menu "bsp_illuminate — display pipeline"

    config DISPLAY_LVGL_AVOID_TEAR
        bool "Use panel frame buffers directly (tear-free)"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, esp_lvgl_port sets LVGL's buf1/buf2 to the two DPI
            frame buffers owned by the MIPI-DSI panel and skips its own PSRAM
            buffer allocation. Requires num_fbs = 2 in esp_lcd_dpi_panel_config_t.
            Eliminates the per-frame PSRAM->PSRAM memcpy that the fallback
            (separate LVGL buffers + copy into a single DPI FB) performs, and
            removes visible tearing on scroll/animation. Should be combined
            with either DIRECT_MODE (recommended) or FULL_REFRESH.

    config DISPLAY_LVGL_DIRECT_MODE
        bool "LVGL direct mode (dirty-region sync)"
        default y
        help
            LVGL draws into whichever panel FB is currently the back buffer, at
            absolute screen coordinates, and copies only the union of the
            current-frame + prior-frame dirty areas to the other FB after each
            swap. Cheaper per frame than full refresh. Incompatible with LVGL
            sw_rotate (rotation must be identity or performed by the panel).

    config DISPLAY_LVGL_FULL_REFRESH
        bool "LVGL full-refresh mode"
        default n
        help
            LVGL always redraws the entire screen into the back FB. Wastes
            CPU/PPA on unchanged areas but sidesteps dirty-region sync bugs.
            Kept for A/B comparison against direct mode. Mutually exclusive
            with DIRECT_MODE at runtime (esp_lvgl_port picks direct_mode first
            if both are set).

endmenu
